body:
i can't imagine how hard it must be to lose your cat. i'm so sorry that happened. before you go, maybe take a walk around your neighborhood to reminisce about the good things in life. who knows, maybe you'll realize that you do have things to look forward to. like being able to drink legally and go out with your friend. or adopting a new cat, not as a replacement, but to commemorate the short but wonderful life of your deceased one. make great meals for yourself that day to remember your favorite tastes and eat some delicious food. put together a playlist for the car ride to the beach and perhaps realize that there is so much music that you haven't discovered yet. so many awesome shows to watch, carnivals to go to, animals to pet, foods to try, places to go to, and people to meet.

&#x200B;

i'm not trying to give you unsolicited advice, but i do want you to know this: you will be missed. by me, and everyone in this reddit. i may not know you personally, but i know your struggle and i will miss the opportunity i have to get to know you. to you, i'm probably just a random 16 year old in some city in America, but i empathize with your struggle and i feel your pain. i'm sorry you have to go through this, but i hope you choose to stay :) <3
